<title>UK: Amoco halts gas output at four North Sea fields.</title>
<headline>Amoco halts gas output at four North Sea fields.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Amoco has suspended gas production at the Indefatigable, Davy, Bessemer and Beaufort fields in the North Sea following a technical problem, a company spokesman said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Production was halted on Wednesday following a problem on the condensate line from the Inde 23 Alpha platform. A spokesman said production is expected to resume on Thursday night.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom, +44 171 542 6412</p>
</text>
